    "body": "The native two-read operator had no ordinary-answer learning connection. This adds offline Rust bridge-only shadows/q4 export and final Copy/Period/Stop marginal loss through observation of the refined native state. Stage1, immutable source keys, value producer and readouts remain fixed. Hard forward uses the checked integer operator; the explicitly biased backward considers all120 exact native right-H4 outcomes without a fake token transition or target-selected read.\n\nActual JointCopy and matched RoleSurface admissions each preserve530 own-prefix predictions and570 canonical identity-feedback positions at parent CE0.492381624865. Both report finite64-episode credit with18,240/79,680 nonzero bridge coordinates and zero optimizer updates. Independent saved-output review passes15,784 checks; all144 result files20,593,788B return with exact SHA/file-set equality. Raw gradient coordinates are not retained, so their aggregate arithmetic/hash is not independently reconstructed. This admits a paired fit, not a learned attention or chat claim.\n\nValidation:13 focused Rust tests and optimized example build on the existing Linux CPU pod; package formatting and claim-wording gate pass. Tests cover finite-action adjoint, identity/aliases/relabeling, Copy/Period/Stop bridge-only credit, an actual0.124→0.125 native quantum crossing and stale-cache rejection, and output isolation. Executed source1b27d2d; delivery changes only documentation and rustfmt module ordering. Failed compile/fixture/storage attempts are retained and separately repaired. Complete120min charge; no GPU/runners/laptop model CPU/new paid provision.\n\nCurrent state and roadmap now specify a prospectively bounded paired bridge-only fit, baseline-inclusive native development ranking and a new untouched transfer frozen before update1. General Generate/compiler/store/session/reasoning and laptop energy remain unfinished. Shared session source is untouched.\n\nReferences #1552. References #1512.\n",
